  term     = {blast radius},
  names    = {vi-blast-radius},
  verdict  = {APPLIES},
  rests-on = {r-crash-only},
  claim    = {\textbf{Blast radius}, and it is already the corpus's own word --- kept here because the reasoning behind it is the transferable part. Where per-device redundancy was unaffordable, the blast radius was FITTED to the redundancy model instead of the other way round: single-supply machines alternated across two power rails so a rail failure cost half a population rather than all of it, and the lone UPS was wired to degrade to raw mains rather than take the load down with it. Designing the failure DOMAIN when you cannot afford to eliminate the failure is the same discipline crash-only recovery formalizes at the software layer},
